# Publish every new app build to GitHub

This is a **must-do** rule (Josh, November 1).

Package every app Josh will run with the one command that also publishes it as
a private GitHub pre-release, so he can use it on his other Macs without
building there. Push the commit to `origin/main` first; the script refuses an
unpushed or dirty checkout.

```sh
bash scripts/package-app.sh <sealed engine-artifacts.json>
```

Tell Josh the release tag. Don't repeat the install caveats (keep the
`development` folder together, ARM64 only, `gh` download avoids quarantine);
he knows them. They're documented in `tests/Packaging/README.md`, "Publishing
app builds", for agents.
